        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e8836059-ad16-5400-b0e2-4b854d49171d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Craig Gillespie, Thomas McCarthy, Steve \"Spaz\" Williams, Ed Decter, John J. Strauss, Mark Gibson, Philip Halprin, Lake Bell, Owen Wilson, Pierce Brosnan\n- Films: Million Dollar Arm, The Wild, No Escape, Over Her Dead Body, What Happens in Vegas, It's Complicated, No Strings Attached, The Secret Life of Pets\n- Television series: Boston Legal, Surface, How to Make It in America, Childrens Hospital\n- Companies: Walt Disney Pictures\n- Topics: film credits, acting roles\n\nFacts:\n- The television series Boston Legal featured Lake Bell from 2004 to 2006.\n- The television series Surface featured Lake Bell from 2005 to 2006.\n- The film The Wild is a 2006 American 3D computer-animated comedy directed by Steve \"Spaz\" Williams and written by Ed Decter, John J. Strauss, Mark Gibson, and Philip Halprin.\n- The television series Childrens Hospital featured Lake Bell from 2008 to 2016.\n- Lake Bell appeared in the films Over Her Dead Body and What Happens in Vegas in 2008.\n- Lake Bell appeared in the film It's Complicated in 2009.\n- The television series How to Make It in America featured Lake Bell from 2010 to 2011.\n- Lake Bell appeared in the film No Strings Attached in 2011.\n- The film Million Dollar Arm is a 2014 American biographical sports drama directed by Craig Gillespie, produced by Walt Disney Pictures, and written by Thomas McCarthy.\n- Lake Bell appeared in the film Million Dollar Arm in 2014.\n- The 2015 film No Escape stars Owen Wilson, Lake Bell, and Pierce Brosnan and follows an expat engineer trapped with his family during a violent uprising in an unnamed Southeast Asian country.\n- Lake Bell appeared in the film The Secret Life of Pets in 2016.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6ee51da9-fb70-56f9-82d5-1142046ea4b4",
        "text": "Page: Million Dollar Arm. Sentence: Million Dollar Arm is a 2014 American biographical sports drama film directed by Craig Gillespie and produced by Walt Disney Pictures from a screenplay written by Thomas McCarthy.\nPage: The Wild. Sentence: The Wild is a 2006 American 3D computer animated comedy directed by animator Steve \"Spaz\" Williams, and written by Ed Decter, John J. Strauss, Mark Gibson and Philip Halprin.\nPage: Lake Bell. Sentence: She has starred in various television series, including \"Boston Legal\" (2004–2006), \"Surface\" (2005–2006), \"How to Make It in America\" (2010–2011) and \"Childrens Hospital\" (2008–2016), and in films including \"Over Her Dead Body\" (2008), \"What Happens in Vegas\" (2008), \"It's Complicated\" (2009), \"No Strings Attached\" (2011), \"Million Dollar Arm\" (2014) and \"The Secret Life of Pets\" (2016).\nPage: No Escape (2015 film). Sentence: The film stars Owen Wilson, Lake Bell, and Pierce Brosnan, and tells the story of an expat engineer trapped with his family in an unnamed South-East Asian country during a violent uprising.",
